# UI Patterns

## Page Names

| File | Class | Purpose |
|------|-------|---------|
| `home_page.dart` | `HomePage` | Home tab with Verse/Hadith of the Day, search, continue reading, explore |
| `quran_page.dart` | `QuranPage` | Quran tab: surah list with Surah/Juz/Makki-Madani/Revelation tabs |
| `surah_reader_page.dart` | `SurahReaderPage` | Full-screen surah reading with scrubber + settings sheet |
| `hadith_page.dart` | `HadithPage` | Hadith tab: all books from all collections |
| `hadith_reader_page.dart` | `HadithReaderPage` | Full-screen hadith reading with scrubber + settings sheet |
| `bookmarks_page.dart` | `BookmarksPage` | Bookmarks tab |
| `settings_page.dart` | `SettingsPage` | Settings tab |
| `global_search_page.dart` | `SearchPage` | Full-screen global search |
| `tajweed_guide_page.dart` | `TajweedGuidePage` | Full-screen tajweed colour legend & rules guide |
| `app_shell.dart` | `AppShell` | Bottom nav shell (6 tabs) |

## Navigation

```dart
// Switch to a tab
context.go('/quran');

// Push a detail page (full screen, no bottom nav)
context.push('/quran/1');
context.push('/quran/2?ayah=255');
context.push('/hadith/forties/nawawi40.json?title=Nawawi%2040');
context.push('/search');
```

## Key Architecture Rules

- **Cache futures in `initState()`** -- NEVER create futures inside `build()`. This causes re-fetching on every rebuild and UI flickering.
- **Do not save last-read from `build()`** -- Use a `_hasPersistedLastRead` flag for the initial write. Scroll updates use a debounce and `notify: false` so the reader does not rebuild.
- **Scroll-to only once** -- Use a `_hasScrolledToAyah` flag to prevent repeated scrolling on rebuilds.
- Detail pages push full-screen via `parentNavigatorKey` (hides bottom nav)

## Scope Access

- Font zoom: `SettingsScope.of(context).arabicZoom` / `.englishZoom`
- Theme: `AppScope.of(context).setAppearance(...)`
- Bookmarks: `BookmarkScope.of(context)`
- Theme mode: `Theme.of(context).brightness`

## Reader Pages (SurahReaderPage, HadithReaderPage)

Both reader pages share these features:
- **In-page search**: Search icon opens a text field that filters items within the current surah/book (NOT global search)
- **Settings bottom sheet**: Gear icon opens `ReaderSettingsSheet` for live font size, appearance, and show-translation
- **Scroll scrubber**: Custom `ScrollScrubber` overlaid on the right edge, works with `ItemScrollController`/`ItemPositionsListener`
- **Bookmarking**: Per-ayah (Quran) or per-hadith toggle
- **Auto-save**: Last-read position saved on open and as you scroll (`notify: false`)

### Surah Reader specifics
- **App bar:** Info (surah details), Quran Reading & Tajweed guide (book icon → `showQuranReadingGuideSheet()`), in-page search, settings
- Bismillah header for all surahs except Al-Fatiha (1) and At-Tawbah (9)
- Arabic with tajweed coloring
- Tajweed legend at the bottom
- **Word-by-word** (when `settings.wordByWordEnabled`): ayah Arabic renders via `WordByWordArabicText`; tapping a word tints it and shows `WordGlossCard` floating at the bottom of the screen. Only one word is selected at a time across the surah, and the card floats so revealing a meaning never shifts the text being read. Search results stay plain.

### Hadith Reader specifics
- Narrator shown in a distinct container
- Arabic without tajweed
- Chapter dividers above the first hadith of each chapter
- Chapter jump sheet from the app bar list icon when the book has more than one chapter

## QuranPage Groupings

`QuranPage` has a `TabBar` with 4 views:
- **Surah** (default): Flat list of 114 surahs
- **Juz**: Grouped by Juz 1-30 with section headers
- **Type**: Two sections (Meccan, Medinan)
- **Revelation**: Sorted by chronological revelation order

Each surah card: left = number badge + English name (and translation on some tabs); center = Arabic surah name (vowelled, big and bold); right = ayah count. Makki/Madani badge (amber/teal). No CDN or first-ayah images — Arabic text only.

## Hadith Page (Tab)

- Search bar always visible; collection chips (All / Forties / Nine Books / Other)
- **Start here** row for the three 40-hadith collections when browsing All
- Continue-reading banner when `lastReadHadith` exists
- Compact numbered book rows (count, resume chip, bookmark, about sheet)
- Summaries live in the about sheet (info icon / long-press), not on the card
- Tapping a book opens HadithReaderPage

## Home Page

- Verse of the Day card (deep indigo gradient)
- Hadith of the Day card (emerald gradient)
- Continue Reading cards
- Explore tiles (Quran, Hadith)

## Reusable Widgets

- `ArabicText` -- Arabic rendering with optional Tajweed coloring (uses `tajweedSpans()` internally)
- `arabicTextStyle()` / `arabicStrutStyle()` -- shared Qur'anic typography in `arabic_text.dart`. Anything drawing Arabic must use these instead of assembling its own `TextStyle`, so font choice and fallbacks stay in one place.
- `WordByWordArabicText` -- tappable per-word Arabic that preserves tajweed colours; selection is shown with a background tint
- `WordGlossCard` -- floating bottom card showing the tapped word's Arabic and English
- `tajweedSpans()` -- Public API in `lib/ui/widgets/tajweed.dart` that converts raw Qur'anic text into colour-coded `InlineSpan`s. Also exposes `tajweedColorAssignments()` for unit testing without `BuildContext`.
- `GradientTile` -- Card with gradient background, icon, title, subtitle
- `ReaderSettingsSheet` -- Bottom sheet for reader font/theme settings (`showReaderSettingsSheet()`)
- `HadithChapterSheet` -- Chapter table of contents for the hadith reader (`showHadithChapterSheet()`)
- `ScrollScrubber` -- Draggable vertical scrubber for `ScrollablePositionedList`

## Animations

Uses `flutter_animate` for:
- Staggered fade+slide list entry animations on QuranPage and HadithPage
- Fade+slide on Verse/Hadith of the Day cards
- Keep delays short (30ms per item, capped at 600ms) for responsiveness
